No `LoopContext` is created. `visit_For` asks three questions at compile time — is the loop recursive, does the body mention `loop`, does it contain a scoped block (compiler.py#L1184-1189) — and all three answered no, so `extended_loop` stayed `False` and a plain Python loop was emitted (compiler.py#L1249-1272). The emitted code is:

```
for l_1_user in (undefined(name='users') if l_0_users is missing else l_0_users):
    _loop_vars = {}
```

with `l_0_users = resolve('users')` hoisted to the top of `block_content`.
